    /// <summary>
    /// A dressed event's `Id.Entry` -> the image the default event layout
    /// draws for it until one of its own is supplied (EB-764).
    ///
    /// `EventModel.InitialPortraitPath` is `ImageHelper.GetImagePath(
    /// "events/" + Id.Entry.ToLowerInvariant() + ".png")` -- DERIVED from
    /// the id, `private`, and not virtual -- so a dressed event asks the
    /// pack for a path nothing produces and `NEventLayout.InitializeVisuals`
    /// threw `AssetLoadException` before the page was drawn. The value is the
    /// BASE event's own image, which is the same borrowing
    /// `TeyvatFrame.AssetAlias` makes for a dressing's backgrounds, and it
    /// retires the same way: `Patches/EventPortraitPatch` asks
    /// `ResourceLoader.Exists` of the DRESSED path first, so a real portrait
    /// dropped at `events/&lt;dressed entry&gt;.png` wins with no code change.
    ///
    /// GENERATED, so a dressed event cannot exist without a portrait row --
    /// which is exactly the shape EB-764 was.
    /// </summary>
